post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'

POWERarm installed.

  Getting started:
    POWERarmRootFSFetcher         # fetch/extract a RootFS
    POWERarm /path/to/binary      # run a guest executable
    POWERarmBash                  # a bash running under emulation
    POWERarmConfig                # GUI for per-application settings

  Gaming notes, per-title workarounds and tuning:
    /usr/share/doc/powerarm/GAMING.md

  The binfmt_misc handler for AArch64 ELF binaries is installed to
  /usr/lib/binfmt.d. Activate them with:
    systemctl restart systemd-binfmt

  Library thunks (native host GL/Vulkan/wayland passthrough) are installed
  and enabled system-wide via /usr/share/powerarm/Config.json. Disable or
  tune them per user (~/.config/powerarm/Config.json) or per app (POWERarmConfig).

  Note: the SMC (self-modifying code) mtrack path needs a 4K-page kernel.
  On a 64K-page kernel FEX falls back to a slower software path.

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'

binfmt_misc handlers were removed. Run
  systemctl restart systemd-binfmt
to drop the registrations from the running kernel.

EOF
}
